S", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.7758, "filing_name": "Morgan Stanley 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/895421/000089542126000086/ms-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MS_10K_2025-12-31__mdna__0878", "ticker": "MS", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.7734, "filing_name": "Morgan Stanley 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/895421/000089542126000086/ms-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MS_10K_2025-12-31__mdna__0225", "ticker": "MS", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.7722, "filing_name": "Morgan Stanley 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/895421/000089542126000086/ms-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MS_10K_2025-12-31__mdna__0201", "ticker": "MS", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.7714, "filing_name": "Morgan Stanley 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/895421/000089542126000086/ms-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MS_10K_2025-12-31__mdna__0175", "ticker": "MS", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.7602, "filing_name": "Morgan Stanley 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/895421/000089542126000086/ms-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MS_10K_2025-12-31__mdna__0174", "ticker": "MS", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.7521, "filing_name": "Morgan Stanley 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/895421/000089542126000086/ms-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}, {"chunk_id": "MS_10K_2025-12-31__mdna__0181", "ticker": "MS", "form": "10-K", "fiscal_label": "FY2025", "period_end": "2025-12-31", "section": "mdna", "score": 0.75, "filing_name": "Morgan Stanley 10-K FY2025", "sec_url": "https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/895421/000089542126000086/ms-20251231.htm", "truncated": false}], "collapsed_near_duplicates": 51, "dropped_candidates": 563, "token_estimate": 31972, "gaps": [], "degraded": []}, "answer": {"direct_answer": "All four banks tie regulatory capital risk to restrictions on shareholder distributions. JPMorgan (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025) says failing to maintain required capital, or using its buffers, could reduce permitted share repurchases and constrain common dividends [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0043]. Bank of America (fiscal 2024, ended December 31, 2024) says regulators may change capital requirements, including TLAC, and how RWA is calculated, and that a subsidiary losing well-capitalized status could restrict dividends and repurchases [BAC_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0061]. Goldman Sachs (fiscal 2024, ended December 31, 2024) says the SCB has led to higher and more volatile Standardized capital ratio requirements, and expects its G-SIB surcharge to rise from 3.0% to 3.5% effective January 1, 2026 [GS_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0064]. Morgan Stanley (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025) describes the SCB mechanics and notes that banking agencies can prohibit or limit dividends and other capital actions [MS_10K_2025-12-31__mdna__0201] [MS_10K_2025-12-31__unknown__0097]. The filings do not rank these risks.", "company_findings": [{"ticker": "JPM", "company": "JPMorgan Chase & Co", "findings": [{"point": "Its stated drivers of capital pressure include RWA increases and higher Federal Reserve CCAR stress-loss estimates that could increase its SCB (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0043"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Falling below requirements or unfavorable capital rule changes could reduce repurchases, constrain dividends, and curtail business activities or operations.", "citations": ["JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0043"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "If regulators do not approve its models for market, credit and operational risk RWA under Basel III, it could face higher capital charges.", "citations": ["JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0071"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "BAC", "company": "Bank of America Corporation", "findings": [{"point": "As a G-SIB it must hold a G-SIB surcharge, an SCB and a countercyclical buffer, reassessed at least annually (fiscal 2024, ended December 31, 2024).", "citations": ["BAC_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0061"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "If a subsidiary bank loses well-capitalized status, the Federal Reserve can require an agreement restricting activities such as dividends and repurchases, with more severe restrictions if it fails to comply.", "citations": ["BAC_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0061"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Regulators may change TLAC, long-term debt and RWA calculation rules, and 2023 proposals on RWA and the G-SIB surcharge may be re-proposed.", "citations": ["BAC_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0061"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "GS", "company": "Goldman Sachs Group Inc", "findings": [{"point": "The SCB has replaced the capital conservation buffer, producing higher and more volatile Standardized ratio requirements; non-compliance could limit repurchases, dividends and discretionary pay (fiscal 2024, ended December 31, 2024).", "citations": ["GS_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0064"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "Its G-SIB surcharge has risen with business expansion, balance sheet growth and short-term wholesale funding, and is expected to increase from 3.0% to 3.5% effective January 1, 2026.", "citations": ["GS_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0064"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "It may face higher requirements from the Basel Committee's finalization of post-crisis capital reforms, and ring-fencing and internal TLAC rules limit its ability to move capital among entities.", "citations": ["GS_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0063", "GS_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0028"], "unverified": false}]}, {"ticker": "MS", "company": "Morgan Stanley", "findings": [{"point": "U.S. banking agencies can prohibit or limit dividends or other capital actions, and the filing refers to a risk factor on regulatory constraints or revised capital requirements (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025).", "citations": ["MS_10K_2025-12-31__unknown__0097"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "The Federal Reserve sets an SCB annually from supervisory stress test results, with a 2.5% floor, taking effect from October 1.", "citations": ["MS_10K_2025-12-31__mdna__0201"], "unverified": false}, {"point": "It must remain well-capitalized to remain an FHC and must maintain minimum risk-based, leverage-based and TLAC ratios.", "citations": ["MS_10K_2025-12-31__mdna__0175"], "unverified": false}]}], "comparison_table": {"columns": ["Company (fiscal period)", "Capital rule drivers cited", "Stated consequence"], "rows": [["JPM (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025)", "RWA growth, CCAR stress losses raising SCB [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0043]", "Reduced repurchases, constrained dividends [JPM_10K_2025-12-31__risk_factors__0043]"], ["BAC (fiscal 2024, ended December 31, 2024)", "G-SIB surcharge, SCB, countercyclical buffer, TLAC changes [BAC_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0061]", "Restrictions on dividends and repurchases [BAC_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0061]"], ["GS (fiscal 2024, ended December 31, 2024)", "SCB volatility; G-SIB surcharge 3.0% to 3.5% [GS_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0064]", "Limits on repurchases, dividends, discretionary pay [GS_10K_2024-12-31__risk_factors__0064]"], ["MS (fiscal 2025, ended December 31, 2025)", "Annual SCB from stress test, 2.5% floor [MS_10K_2025-12-31__mdna__0201]", "Agencies may limit dividends and capital actions [MS_10K_2025-